From: Salt OpenWrt packaging
Subject: [PATCH] loader: discover adjacent sourceless Python bytecode

The OpenWrt package compiles Salt with the target SDK Python using
compileall -b, then deletes the .py sources. The resulting modules are
stored as salt/modules/foo.pyc, not inside __pycache__ directories.

Salt 3008.3 already knows how to load sourceless bytecode, but LazyLoader
skips these adjacent .pyc files while discovering plugins. Remove that
skip so the installed bytecode-only minion can discover its modules.

This changes discovery only; importlib still checks the bytecode header.
Keep upstream source precedence and __pycache__ support for custom modules
synchronized from a master, which may still arrive as Python source.

--- a/salt/loader/lazy.py
+++ b/salt/loader/lazy.py
@@ -730,12 +730,6 @@
                             # exists, so skip this.
                             continue
 
-                    if not dirname and ext == ".pyc":
-                        # On Python 3, we should only load .pyc files from the
-                        # __pycache__ subdirectory (i.e. when dirname is not an
-                        # empty string).
-                        continue
-
                     # Made it this far - add it
                     self.file_mapping[f_noext] = (fpath, ext, opt_index)
 
